((kind . tasks-my)
 (tasks .
  (("IDEA-CARGO-CHECK" . ((priority . 0.8) (capabilities . (rust))
                          (description . "rustc/indexmap/webkitgtk blockers resolved, commit 0d326ff. Remaining: my-idea's build.rs (tauri-build::acl::app_manifest_permissions -> tauri_utils::acl::build::define_permissions, tauri-utils-2.9.3/src/acl/build.rs:68-98) fails with bare EPERM. Traced the exact call site by reading source (no strace available): the failing write is out_dir.join(pkg_name+'-permission-files') via write_if_changed (plain fs::read+fs::write, nothing exotic) OR the glob::glob(pattern).flat_map(canonicalize) chain immediately before it. Ruled out: DrvFs vs native WSL ext4 (identical failure on both via CARGO_TARGET_DIR redirect), missing ./permissions/autogenerated dir (pre-created manually, error persists at the same point). Also noteworthy but unconfirmed as related: autogenerate_command_permissions writes to a RELATIVE './permissions/autogenerated' path (tauri-build acl.rs:~277), always resolving under src-tauri/ on DrvFs regardless of CARGO_TARGET_DIR — a real fragility even if not this bug's cause. Next step needs an actual strace/ltrace to pin the syscall; source-reading is exhausted. Not done — cargo check still does not pass."))))))
